# Managed alongside cpu-watchdog (see /etc/cpu-watchdog.conf, Layer 4).
#
# SIGTERM when available RAM <= 6% AND free swap <= 10% of totals;
# SIGKILL at 3% / 5%. Reacts in ~1s, protecting against the kernel OOM killer,
# which once killed systemd, dbus and the main service instead of the dozens
# of claude/node/php sessions that were exhausting memory.
#
# --prefer: node/php/chrome run vite, jest, phpunit and headless browsers
#           launched by agents for testing. Claude Code sessions are deliberately
#           excluded: they are selected later based on size.
# --avoid:  remote access, init, container runtimes and databases.
# cpu-watchdog reports kills to Telegram (Layer 4c).
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-m 6,3 -s 10,5 -r 3600 --prefer '^(node|php|php8[.]3|chrome|chrome-devtools)$' --avoid '^(sshd|systemd|systemd-.*|init|dbus-daemon|dockerd|containerd|containerd-shim|postgres|qdrant|tailscaled|earlyoom|cpulimit)$'"
